round is a very simple and helpful function used in order to round a number.
here is an example of round:
round(3.14159, 2)

the 3.14159 is the first value, wich describes the number wich you would like to round.
the 2 is the second value, wich describes to wich decimal. 
2 would mean the SECOND decimal, wich would round this number to 3.14. 
4 would mean the FOURTH decimal, wich would round the number to 3.1416.

but, the second value is not needed.
if you do not put anything for the second value, than it will round to the nearest whole integer. In this case, 3.

hope you have fun with the round function!
